        "summary":  "A Harvard/MIT/University of Washington study of 228 evaluators found that AI recommendation systems were accepted 67% of the time overall, but counterintuitively, AI explanations with narrative reasoning caused worse decision outcomes than black-box recommendations. Reviewers given narrative AI explanations disproportionately deferred to incorrect decisions, suppressing independent judgment through \u0027ready-made justifications.\u0027 The research team attributes this to LLMs\u0027 ability to generate fluent, expert-sounding rationales that create an \u0027illusion of explanatory depth.\u0027",
