        "summary":  "A Thoughtworks survey of 3,200 global CIOs found that AI governance authority is fragmented across enterprises, with 88% of respondents saying AI adoption is moving faster than governance structures can keep pace. Critically, 94% of U.S. CIOs said their team would be held responsible for security or compliance failures triggered by AI tools deployed by other business units. Nearly one in five senior leaders admitted to pretending to understand AI better than they do.",
